WEBVTT

00:31.114 --> 00:33.950
THE TRUNK

00:34.034 --> 00:38.621
LATE SO HYE-YEONG

01:17.452 --> 01:20.205
This is a pretty lonely
memorial service, isn't it?

01:24.334 --> 01:26.169
I'm sorry for leaving you all alone.

01:28.379 --> 01:29.881
If we ever meet again…

01:31.966 --> 01:33.802
I'll make sure to stay by your side.

01:38.807 --> 01:40.308
I won't leave you by yourself.

01:49.734 --> 01:51.111
Were there a lot of people?

01:51.945 --> 01:52.779
Yes.

01:53.655 --> 01:54.656
Yeah, right.

01:55.740 --> 01:57.826
We're all Hye-yeong had.
Who else would come?

01:59.994 --> 02:01.454
I'm sorry I couldn't make it.

02:02.539 --> 02:04.332
It's not like you missed it on purpose.

02:06.751 --> 02:07.669
It's fine.

02:50.879 --> 02:53.339
YEONHEE UNIVERSITY
GRADUATION GOWN AND CAP RENTALS

03:31.961 --> 03:33.087
Did someone pass away?

03:37.592 --> 03:38.426
A friend.

03:40.303 --> 03:42.847
Do people wear mourning hairpins
even when friends pass?

03:48.228 --> 03:49.437
She had no family.

03:51.272 --> 03:52.941
Also, it feels like I killed her.

03:54.525 --> 03:55.360
How about you?

03:59.155 --> 04:00.240
My mom passed.

04:06.037 --> 04:07.538
I also feel like I killed her.

04:31.729 --> 04:32.563
You probably

04:33.982 --> 04:35.650
weren't the reason she died.

04:46.077 --> 04:48.997
HAN JEONG-WON

04:49.080 --> 04:55.003
THE TRUNK

06:31.349 --> 06:32.433
Are you all right?

06:35.395 --> 06:36.562
It's not my blood.

06:38.064 --> 06:39.357
How do you know about this place?

06:40.566 --> 06:42.485
This was your address on the contract.

06:59.043 --> 07:00.169
If Eom Tae-seong was here…

07:02.338 --> 07:03.631
Is this the house of that man?

07:04.799 --> 07:06.008
The one your mother killed.

07:09.846 --> 07:11.139
What's it to you?

07:13.808 --> 07:15.601
I'm just worried.

07:15.685 --> 07:17.228
Don't worry about it. Just leave.

07:17.728 --> 07:19.397
This is none of your concern.

07:21.274 --> 07:23.609
Aren't married couples
allowed to be concerned?

07:24.569 --> 07:25.778
You said you're my wife.

07:29.115 --> 07:30.616
You think we have something special?

07:33.077 --> 07:35.163
You're as selfish as ever.

07:35.788 --> 07:36.706
And so childish.

07:38.332 --> 07:39.917
Why must it always be your way?

07:42.587 --> 07:44.547
I just did my duty.

07:44.630 --> 07:46.466
It's part of the job, in the manual.

07:46.549 --> 07:49.594
The only reason I grilled fish
and cooked every morning

07:50.094 --> 07:52.555
is so you could experience
a sense of normalcy.

07:53.139 --> 07:54.557
So don't overstep.

07:57.018 --> 07:59.437
Does curating the perfect marriage
fill you with pride?

08:00.688 --> 08:03.024
Here you are, unable to leave this house.

08:04.358 --> 08:07.945
Does the pride you feel
from saving others lessen your guilt?

08:09.947 --> 08:12.325
You're also a part
of such a conceited marriage.

08:14.160 --> 08:17.288
So there's no reason for you to be here,
worrying about me.

08:18.831 --> 08:20.458
Stop meddling in my affairs.

08:21.792 --> 08:25.129
Eom Tae-seong or not,
this has nothing to do with you!

08:28.049 --> 08:30.176
If you understand, leave.
This is my space.

08:31.969 --> 08:33.679
You know it's not your space.

08:36.432 --> 08:37.850
It's just a hollow shell

08:39.060 --> 08:40.853
that you're still clinging to.

08:47.193 --> 08:49.070
What are you so afraid of?

08:51.364 --> 08:53.866
Are you afraid
that you might actually fall for me?

09:01.332 --> 09:02.166
Just leave.

09:03.376 --> 09:05.294
Go back to your fancy house.

09:55.553 --> 09:56.637
How may I help you?

09:57.847 --> 10:00.725
Anti-inflammatory drugs,
antibiotics, and painkillers.

10:00.808 --> 10:04.103
Antiseptics and bandages.
Give me the strongest ones you've got.

10:04.895 --> 10:06.606
How were you injured?

10:06.689 --> 10:09.525
Let's say I had an accident
with a screwdriver.

10:10.026 --> 10:12.695
It'd be better to go to the ER.

10:13.195 --> 10:16.949
This bitch must be fucking joking.

10:21.329 --> 10:24.832
Just give them to me, okay?

10:25.333 --> 10:27.710
Give me the meds!

10:43.017 --> 10:45.978
Mr. Seo Do-ha, you sure have changed.

10:47.271 --> 10:49.523
This is so out of character for you.

10:50.983 --> 10:51.901
You're the one

10:53.027 --> 10:54.528
who made me like this.

10:55.196 --> 10:58.991
Did you think that I wouldn't know
what you did five years ago?

11:01.160 --> 11:03.329
You knew I was the one
who sent those clips?

11:04.830 --> 11:06.415
Noh In-ji's mom did everything.

11:06.916 --> 11:09.627
I just acted in the public interest
and sent her a tip.

11:11.087 --> 11:11.921
Wait.

11:12.004 --> 11:13.339
If I kill you and disappear,

11:14.256 --> 11:15.466
it would all be over.

11:16.676 --> 11:18.386
Show your face here again,

11:19.428 --> 11:20.429
and you die.

11:42.535 --> 11:43.411
Ma'am,

11:44.453 --> 11:45.705
have I done something wrong?

11:47.248 --> 11:49.125
Look. I'm hurt.

11:53.170 --> 11:54.088
Look, lady.

11:56.966 --> 11:58.384
Have I done anything to you?

12:02.346 --> 12:03.639
For fuck's sake.

12:13.274 --> 12:14.650
It won't come out.

12:15.401 --> 12:18.654
Anyway, things don't look great here.

12:20.030 --> 12:21.073
Right, I understand.

12:22.700 --> 12:23.868
Hey, hang up.

12:37.631 --> 12:38.966
Is this Eom Tae-seong's blood?

12:41.427 --> 12:43.471
Good God, so it is.

12:45.306 --> 12:47.057
I finally get to see your face.

12:48.768 --> 12:51.437
I'm Ms. Do-dam. I live next door.

12:51.520 --> 12:55.149
I know In-ji well enough to know
she's been brooding here for five years

12:58.027 --> 12:59.945
How long has this been going on?

13:00.029 --> 13:01.530
You took your time showing up.

13:01.614 --> 13:04.241
Why not ask once she's bloody dead?
For heaven's sake.

13:06.744 --> 13:11.749
I heard that Eom Tae-seong's
been clinging to In-ji and harassing her.

13:12.625 --> 13:14.543
I also heard that he killed someone.

13:28.516 --> 13:29.350
Frustrating.

13:30.810 --> 13:31.644
So frustrating.

15:07.907 --> 15:09.366
Manual, my ass.

15:20.794 --> 15:22.880
Strawberries used to be a luxury for me,

15:24.089 --> 15:25.925
but now I dig in without a second thought.

15:29.261 --> 15:30.971
I mindlessly gorge myself on them.

15:35.017 --> 15:36.435
He told me to have the baby,

15:37.770 --> 15:39.897
but he won't be involved at all.

15:40.648 --> 15:42.816
I thanked him
and said he'll never see us again.

15:44.068 --> 15:45.235
That's great to hear.

15:47.321 --> 15:48.989
I've been on the run all my life,

15:50.616 --> 15:52.534
but I finally feel like
I've put down roots.

15:53.410 --> 15:55.996
I'm going to have this baby
and raise it well.

15:56.997 --> 15:58.290
It's a jungle out there,

15:58.374 --> 16:01.001
and if the baby takes after me,
they'll be a handful…

16:03.045 --> 16:04.630
but I want them to be happy.

16:09.551 --> 16:11.261
By the way, you don't look so great.

16:13.430 --> 16:15.015
I had an argument with my husband.

16:15.766 --> 16:16.892
You actually argue?

16:18.394 --> 16:20.062
He said that I was afraid.

16:21.021 --> 16:25.693
Big words from a guy
who's never left that house of his.

16:33.075 --> 16:35.536
You can stop looking for him now.

16:36.912 --> 16:37.746
Why's that?

16:38.789 --> 16:39.665
He came back.

16:40.791 --> 16:41.792
Did you meet with him?

16:44.753 --> 16:48.090
Do you feel like running away
now that you can finally meet him again?

16:52.094 --> 16:53.971
You are afraid, Ms. Noh.

17:05.482 --> 17:09.820
She waited five years in that house
for a guy who might never return.

17:10.404 --> 17:11.947
Do you also think I overstepped?

17:12.948 --> 17:17.036
She has no idea how stubborn she can be
or how much danger she's in right now.

17:18.495 --> 17:20.789
She's so full of herself.

17:21.915 --> 17:25.335
She literally moved into my house,
so why can't I visit hers?

17:26.628 --> 17:29.965
Why does she cling to that house
like her life depends on it?

17:30.549 --> 17:33.761
Why are you getting so worked up?
Who are you to her anyway?

17:41.518 --> 17:45.689
Something came up, so I left early.
I'm sorry about yesterday. I went too far.

17:48.025 --> 17:48.859
What is it?

17:49.443 --> 17:50.319
What did she say?

17:52.613 --> 17:53.864
She said she's sorry.

17:53.947 --> 17:55.199
That settles that, no?

17:58.452 --> 17:59.828
I'm not mad at her.

18:02.372 --> 18:03.665
I'm worried about her.

18:12.549 --> 18:16.261
We've tightened security in the area.
Shall we do the same for your house?

18:17.513 --> 18:19.348
Please install cameras inside the house.

18:21.058 --> 18:22.392
Are you sure that'll be okay?

18:23.185 --> 18:24.603
Yes. Please do it.

18:46.458 --> 18:49.461
I think it's my destiny
to perish alongside Ms. In-ji.

18:49.545 --> 18:51.338
If I can't have her…

18:54.007 --> 18:55.342
maybe that wouldn't be so bad.

19:08.605 --> 19:11.233
The bloodstains aren't Seo Do-ha's.

19:12.526 --> 19:14.361
Ms. Do-dam saw him, and he looked fine.

19:15.487 --> 19:17.239
I guess he wasn't the victim.

19:19.741 --> 19:22.411
You should at least see the jerk.

19:23.996 --> 19:25.414
I'll take care of it.

19:25.497 --> 19:27.124
You'll deal with it? As if.

19:27.207 --> 19:29.918
When you first told me
about that weird marriage thing,

19:30.419 --> 19:34.506
I figured you were doing what you could
to live despite your broken heart.

19:35.883 --> 19:37.885
After my mom and dad got divorced,

19:38.844 --> 19:40.679
my aunts took turns raising me.

19:40.762 --> 19:43.557
I lived like an orphan for five years,
walking on eggshells,

19:45.017 --> 19:48.270
and only learned what family was
when I met you guys in high school.

19:50.189 --> 19:51.857
Hye-yeong actually was an orphan,

19:52.774 --> 19:55.194
and you cut ties with your mom in college.

19:55.986 --> 19:58.488
Until Hye-yeong died,
the three of us would say,

19:58.572 --> 20:01.950
"Who needs marriage
when we're already a perfect family?"

20:02.701 --> 20:04.244
She's the bitch for dying.

20:05.120 --> 20:06.330
A disloyal bitch.

20:12.920 --> 20:15.589
My aunt was insufferable
until the moment she croaked.

20:16.590 --> 20:18.550
My biggest regret
is having stayed by her deathbed

20:19.176 --> 20:21.553
instead of attending Hye-yeong's funeral.

20:22.804 --> 20:26.433
My point is,
I'm the only family you've got.

20:26.516 --> 20:29.228
I know the marriage must end
once you end things with Seo Do-ha.

20:31.021 --> 20:32.022
It's just work.

20:33.523 --> 20:34.358
Come on!

20:35.525 --> 20:36.902
You think I don't know you?

20:37.653 --> 20:39.780
I can tell if your tears
are from sadness or anger

20:39.863 --> 20:41.406
just by looking at your puffy eyes.

20:41.490 --> 20:44.409
You used to be so withdrawn,
but with Han Jeong-won, you're like a--

20:45.244 --> 20:46.578
You've fallen for him!

20:50.916 --> 20:52.876
There's nothing for you to worry about.

20:53.377 --> 20:55.128
It'll be over once the contract ends.

21:36.461 --> 21:38.797
Might as well join me
if you haven't had dinner yet.

21:49.975 --> 21:51.727
What are you doing here?

21:53.437 --> 21:54.563
Where's Ms. Noh In-ji?

21:57.399 --> 21:58.483
I see she's not here.

22:00.027 --> 22:01.320
Say what you want to say.

22:04.906 --> 22:06.908
I have a question for you.

22:07.868 --> 22:10.162
How did you feel
when you first saw Ms. Noh In-ji?

22:15.125 --> 22:17.919
Haven't you ever wondered
why it had to be Noh In-ji?

22:26.845 --> 22:28.680
It can't just be a coincidence.

22:32.059 --> 22:33.393
What are you getting at?

22:37.731 --> 22:39.566
I didn't like those slippers.

22:51.453 --> 22:52.371
Take them off.

23:00.087 --> 23:01.671
You're not really wearing those, are you?

23:04.383 --> 23:05.675
Wear these.

23:24.152 --> 23:27.531
Everything became clear to me
when I saw Noh In-ji's face at NM.

23:28.448 --> 23:30.992
I couldn't stomach
the idea of being with you,

23:32.411 --> 23:35.831
but for the first time,
I felt I could find my way back to you.

23:38.208 --> 23:41.128
That was the reason you picked her?

23:45.757 --> 23:48.385
I thought I was the only one broken,
but I was wrong.

23:49.886 --> 23:51.888
You're the one who's truly broken.

23:54.307 --> 23:56.560
That's why you should end
this fake marriage.

23:57.978 --> 24:00.272
Won't it just break us even further?

24:02.274 --> 24:03.191
I'll be leaving now.

24:04.192 --> 24:05.652
Enjoy your dinner, honey.

24:32.387 --> 24:34.598
You'll find the alimony
to your satisfaction.

24:34.681 --> 24:36.558
We broke the contract, after all.

24:37.142 --> 24:38.935
How about a settlement instead?

24:39.603 --> 24:42.189
We could take you to court

24:42.272 --> 24:45.442
for supplying drugs
and conducting illegal surveillance.

24:46.318 --> 24:47.611
Why haven't you told him?

24:50.447 --> 24:51.740
He didn't seem to know yet.

24:52.908 --> 24:55.911
Because I don't know
how to break it to him yet.

24:58.246 --> 25:01.416
Don't get me wrong.
It wasn't out of consideration for you.

25:02.209 --> 25:04.544
I guess
you don't want to see him get hurt.

25:05.504 --> 25:07.255
That doesn't make you any less fake.

25:07.839 --> 25:11.301
Aren't you here because you're worried
the fake relationship might become real?

25:36.076 --> 25:39.371
You haven't watched soccer in a while.
Is now really the time?

25:40.789 --> 25:43.041
If you want to watch it with me,
just say so.

25:45.627 --> 25:46.962
Who says I do?

26:01.768 --> 26:03.520
I'm sorry for calling you childish.

26:04.312 --> 26:06.523
What about the "selfish as ever" part?

26:07.107 --> 26:09.776
Let's call it even. You said things too.

26:11.152 --> 26:13.613
Didn't you tell me to go back
to my fancy house?

26:14.864 --> 26:16.866
Here we both are in that fancy house.

26:20.036 --> 26:21.371
You hold quite the grudge.

26:21.454 --> 26:22.956
I can recite it word for word.

26:24.541 --> 26:26.042
No one's ever said such things to me.

26:31.089 --> 26:32.632
You were right.

26:36.886 --> 26:38.888
At first, it was out of spite.

26:39.514 --> 26:41.016
Then it was dogged determination.

26:41.641 --> 26:44.060
Towards the end,
I couldn't end things alone,

26:44.686 --> 26:46.146
so I kept watch at the house.

26:48.106 --> 26:50.442
At first, the house was a hollow shell,

26:51.610 --> 26:53.528
but later, that's what I became.

26:56.323 --> 26:58.033
Maybe that's why I couldn't leave.

27:07.709 --> 27:09.085
Once this marriage is over…

27:13.423 --> 27:14.758
will you go back to him?

27:16.843 --> 27:18.970
I wonder
if that's what you're waiting for.

27:21.765 --> 27:23.183
How about you?

27:24.893 --> 27:26.770
Will you go back to Ms. Lee Seo-yeon?

27:47.666 --> 27:48.917
You two are incompatible.

27:50.168 --> 27:51.753
You both know you're miserable,

27:52.462 --> 27:53.463
but you won't admit it.

27:54.547 --> 27:56.007
I'm going back to him.

27:59.094 --> 28:02.263
This NM marriage with me
is what's right for you.

28:03.556 --> 28:04.391
"Right for me"?

28:04.974 --> 28:06.226
We're both mean people.

28:09.521 --> 28:11.231
At least see the contract through.

28:11.731 --> 28:13.566
It's not your fault we're ending things.

28:14.067 --> 28:15.652
I'll explain everything to NM.

28:15.735 --> 28:17.320
That's not my point!

28:18.863 --> 28:22.242
Why do you keep hurting yourself?
Why can't you see reason?

28:27.122 --> 28:27.956
Come over here.

28:35.296 --> 28:36.214
Please.

29:30.435 --> 29:32.896
I guess we should meet.

29:40.153 --> 29:41.321
Let's eat.

30:01.174 --> 30:02.592
I'm heading over to that house.

30:04.886 --> 30:06.179
Will it take long?

30:07.514 --> 30:08.348
No.

30:10.809 --> 30:11.935
Get back safe.

30:56.646 --> 30:58.231
I made some soybean paste soup.

30:58.815 --> 30:59.649
It's ready.

31:00.608 --> 31:01.442
Take a seat.

31:15.498 --> 31:16.332
Dig in.

31:27.886 --> 31:29.721
The soup turned out quite salty.

31:35.393 --> 31:36.895
I know you like egg rolls.

31:47.238 --> 31:49.115
We should have some fresh kimchi too.

31:49.699 --> 31:50.617
Aren't you curious

31:52.327 --> 31:54.829
as to how I've been eating?

31:58.124 --> 32:01.044
I should have used less paste.
It's saltier since it's homemade.

32:01.544 --> 32:02.587
In-ji.

32:03.588 --> 32:04.839
Please stop doing this.

32:08.468 --> 32:10.762
Everything's gone wrong since I met you.

32:11.679 --> 32:13.097
Your mother wasn't to blame.

32:13.806 --> 32:14.766
You were.

32:21.272 --> 32:22.523
We were happy as we were.

32:23.650 --> 32:28.112
We didn't need to change who I was
or gain the approval of others.

32:33.493 --> 32:35.578
Your greed destroyed my life.

32:36.663 --> 32:38.373
Do you still feel like blaming me?

32:39.457 --> 32:41.626
For abandoning you here and leaving?

32:44.045 --> 32:44.879
You're wrong.

32:47.715 --> 32:49.384
I wondered if I was a monster.

32:50.426 --> 32:53.012
On the plane,
after cutting ties with all my loved ones,

32:54.514 --> 32:56.432
I couldn't recognize myself anymore.

32:58.476 --> 33:01.270
The question I most wanted to ask you was,
"Who am I?"

33:04.315 --> 33:06.317
But you were also the one I most feared.

33:08.319 --> 33:09.779
I couldn't bear to face you.

33:11.364 --> 33:13.282
I wanted to blame you for everything,

33:14.450 --> 33:16.035
but doing so would hurt me too.

33:18.413 --> 33:20.164
Why did you do this to me?

33:25.420 --> 33:27.880
Why did you make it impossible
for me to face you?

33:43.062 --> 33:46.441
I thought I wouldn't be able to breathe
if I saw you again…

33:51.029 --> 33:52.363
but I actually can.

33:57.118 --> 33:59.662
At times, I felt so sorry
that I wanted to kill myself.

34:00.830 --> 34:03.416
At others, I hated you so much
that I wanted to kill you.

34:05.001 --> 34:06.461
I would wake up every morning

34:07.795 --> 34:10.965
and pray that my existence
would be erased from the world.

34:11.883 --> 34:16.179
Every day was a living hell,
but I stayed here alone and persevered.

34:19.640 --> 34:20.475
"Today."

34:21.726 --> 34:25.688
"Today's the day he'll come back to me
like nothing ever happened."

34:26.439 --> 34:31.861
One day, two days,
a hundred days, a thousand days…

34:34.489 --> 34:37.158
As time went by,
I started wishing for something else.

34:38.367 --> 34:40.411
That you'd hurry back
and put an end to it.

34:41.996 --> 34:44.165
I couldn't put an end to it by myself,

34:45.333 --> 34:47.085
so I wished that you'd hurry back.

34:49.128 --> 34:51.214
It was like wishing for a merciful death.

34:54.675 --> 34:55.510
But Do-ha…

34:59.097 --> 35:00.765
it's been five years.

35:03.017 --> 35:06.145
How could you take so long
to show yourself?

35:10.024 --> 35:12.318
You should've told me something, anything.

35:13.820 --> 35:18.699
You should have at least told me
that this marriage was over.

35:35.716 --> 35:36.926
I should have…

35:41.264 --> 35:43.224
told you this five years ago.

35:46.352 --> 35:48.437
And I needed to hear this five years ago.

35:51.983 --> 35:53.359
I'm sorry it took so long,

35:54.861 --> 35:55.778
In-ji.

36:07.665 --> 36:08.583
Thank you…

36:13.129 --> 36:15.089
for holding on and staying alive.

36:35.151 --> 36:36.652
- Kick further.
- Further? Okay.

36:36.736 --> 36:37.612
That's it.

36:39.822 --> 36:40.823
Wait, no!

36:44.076 --> 36:47.580
You're supposed to prop me up. That hurts!

36:47.663 --> 36:49.665
He who does the dishes is a good man.

36:51.334 --> 36:53.377
Want me to make tofu stew
with spicy peppers?

36:53.461 --> 36:55.713
Soft tofu stew sounds great.
Damn delicious!

36:55.796 --> 36:56.881
With makgeolli?

36:58.424 --> 36:59.717
That's it.

37:01.594 --> 37:03.512
Have you ever put yourself in my shoes?

37:04.096 --> 37:06.057
When are you going to grow up?

37:06.724 --> 37:10.394
I felt bad for you the first few times.
I even found it endearing.

37:10.478 --> 37:12.939
But now, it's plain annoying.
Just admit you're scared!

37:13.022 --> 37:13.856
You…

37:15.691 --> 37:17.151
you're just like your mother.

37:38.506 --> 37:39.340
Where are you?

37:40.549 --> 37:41.926
I'm worried, so please hurry back.

38:19.213 --> 38:20.548
How did it go?

39:42.880 --> 39:46.008
Were you so sad that it made you
burst into tears like you did?

39:48.010 --> 39:48.844
No.

39:50.679 --> 39:52.139
When I saw your face, I just…

39:57.436 --> 40:00.064
I don't know.
I guess I was glad to see you.

40:03.401 --> 40:07.154
You must be a pervert,
sobbing because you're glad to see me.

40:11.700 --> 40:13.244
I was glad to see you

40:14.870 --> 40:15.746
cry like that.

40:53.576 --> 40:54.452
What do you like?

40:58.706 --> 41:00.124
Which side dishes and stuff.

41:01.959 --> 41:03.461
I'm not really picky.

41:05.588 --> 41:06.714
How about music?

41:10.217 --> 41:12.386
Do you like film soundtracks,

41:13.345 --> 41:14.263
by any chance?

41:18.309 --> 41:19.810
Do you want to come see me work?

41:23.022 --> 41:23.981
Sure.

41:24.940 --> 41:26.525
Tell me when would work, and--

41:26.609 --> 41:27.693
Tomorrow works.

41:30.279 --> 41:31.113
Okay.

41:37.328 --> 41:38.496
Kids, let's eat.

41:38.996 --> 41:41.832
Hwan, Gwan. Come on, your mom's tired.

41:44.001 --> 41:45.336
Get your butts over here!

41:46.212 --> 41:47.296
Sit down and eat.

41:57.348 --> 41:59.391
- Hey, that's mine.
- No, it's mine.

41:59.475 --> 42:01.602
Stay still or you'll get hurt.

42:02.811 --> 42:04.897
- But it's mine!
- Should I start working again?

42:06.482 --> 42:08.901
I just don't think
this is the life I'm meant to live.

42:10.027 --> 42:14.365
On top of all the kids' extracurriculars,
imagine hiring a nanny for school runs.

42:15.074 --> 42:16.784
We'd be in the red for sure.

42:16.867 --> 42:19.787
- I don't want to!
- Hurry up and hand it over.

42:19.870 --> 42:22.206
I know what you want to say.
I hate myself too.

42:23.207 --> 42:25.084
- Give it. That's mine!
- I said no!

42:25.167 --> 42:27.169
- All done. Off you go.
- Let's go!

42:29.088 --> 42:30.297
Let's go!

42:49.858 --> 42:52.403
Are you crying because of what I said
about me finding a job?

42:55.072 --> 42:56.282
Time sure flies.

42:57.283 --> 43:00.828
The kids' toenails used to be so soft,
but now they're so hard.

43:01.579 --> 43:03.414
Clipping them feels completely different.

43:06.834 --> 43:08.294
They'll be adults in no time.

43:08.377 --> 43:11.171
They'll be slamming doors on us
once they hit puberty.

43:13.007 --> 43:14.425
Here come the waterworks.

43:16.677 --> 43:20.347
It's all right, honey.
You have me by your side.

43:30.941 --> 43:32.776
Let's enjoy growing old together, honey.

43:33.277 --> 43:34.153
I love you.

43:34.820 --> 43:35.946
Me too.

43:56.925 --> 43:59.094
The body's been decomposing for a while.

44:00.846 --> 44:04.058
They stuck a sign to the shutters
saying the owner's studying abroad.

44:04.141 --> 44:06.769
The nutter had the balls to kill someone
and then use the printer.

44:07.269 --> 44:08.479
Any security cameras?

44:10.064 --> 44:12.232
We looked at all the footage
from the alley,

44:12.316 --> 44:15.402
but the crazy bastard must have taken
all the pharmacy's footage.

44:16.862 --> 44:18.989
Her neck's been snapped. It's a clean job.

44:19.615 --> 44:20.991
Not a single drop of blood.

44:21.075 --> 44:23.619
The blood we found must be the culprit's.

44:24.536 --> 44:25.621
Send it to forensics,

44:25.704 --> 44:27.998
and run the DNA results
through the database

44:28.082 --> 44:29.208
Yes, sir.

44:35.673 --> 44:37.966
Eom Tae-seong
has been tailing Mr. Han Jeong-won.

44:39.259 --> 44:41.345
They've been frequenting
the same places lately,

44:42.346 --> 44:43.931
which isn't a good sign.

44:47.017 --> 44:48.018
I've notified the company.

44:50.312 --> 44:51.146
I understand.

45:51.290 --> 45:52.124
Hello?

45:56.336 --> 45:57.171
NOH IN-JI

45:57.254 --> 45:58.297
She actually picked up.

46:00.716 --> 46:01.550
Ms. In-ji?

46:04.219 --> 46:05.262
Let's meet.

46:06.722 --> 46:07.556
I'd love that.

46:08.724 --> 46:09.641
When…

46:33.207 --> 46:39.213
NOH IN-JI:
CAFE CAVIAR AT 2 P.M.

47:31.598 --> 47:33.141
I have a question.

47:34.268 --> 47:35.143
I love questions.

47:36.645 --> 47:40.107
Does it make you happy to obsess over me,
harass me, and spy on me?

47:42.860 --> 47:44.862
I don't know who else to ask.

47:49.157 --> 47:51.952
I did some thinking
while I was in the psych ward.

47:53.537 --> 47:56.498
"Noh In-ji could live a better life.
Why does she keep punishing herself?"

47:57.207 --> 48:00.419
"I should let the whole world know
about those fucked up marriages."

48:01.920 --> 48:04.798
Once I decided to do that,
it was like a cloud had lifted.

48:04.882 --> 48:05.716
I felt thrilled.

48:08.886 --> 48:10.512
Was that happiness?

48:15.893 --> 48:17.311
I also have a question for you.

48:18.478 --> 48:20.647
Your marriage contract's
in the trunk, isn't it?

48:22.316 --> 48:25.694
People might not believe me,
but they'll believe material proof.

48:26.445 --> 48:28.655
Once the press and social media
hear about this story,

48:28.739 --> 48:30.282
it's sure to cause a stir.

48:30.365 --> 48:31.199
Don't you think?

48:32.784 --> 48:35.454
I went over to that house
because I thought it was there…

48:38.123 --> 48:39.124
but got stabbed

48:40.042 --> 48:41.251
by Seo Do-ha.

48:43.503 --> 48:47.049
The guy used to be a total loser,
but he's changed.

48:50.260 --> 48:52.220
Thanks to him,
I ended up killing a random person.

48:55.974 --> 48:57.225
Who did you kill?

49:02.814 --> 49:03.941
Why do you hate me?

49:05.442 --> 49:06.777
Do you really have to ask?

49:11.865 --> 49:13.075
I think we're done here.

49:13.951 --> 49:15.202
I have somewhere to be.

49:31.009 --> 49:32.010
Let's leave that out.

49:33.345 --> 49:34.262
This too.

49:34.763 --> 49:36.765
Sounds good. We can just lower this…

49:43.397 --> 49:44.231
What?

49:47.275 --> 49:48.276
What's gotten into him?

49:53.907 --> 49:56.034
You can clock out in five.
I'll wrap up alone today.

49:57.869 --> 49:59.079
That track sounds great.

50:00.497 --> 50:03.959
- What's gotten into him?
- Maybe something good happened.

50:08.880 --> 50:10.841
I'm almost at the underground parking lot.

50:12.551 --> 50:14.511
Wait right there. I'll be down shortly.

50:28.734 --> 50:30.569
What are you doing here,
Mr. Eom Tae-seong?

50:31.570 --> 50:34.197
I never got to hear your answer.

50:38.452 --> 50:39.953
Why do you hate me?

50:42.080 --> 50:46.585
You've hated me from the beginning,
before I'd even done anything.

50:46.668 --> 50:47.919
What I'm asking is,

50:48.754 --> 50:51.214
why would you hate me
from the moment you saw me?

50:52.299 --> 50:54.134
It wasn't like that with Han Jeong-won.

51:00.849 --> 51:02.267
Speaking of him,

51:03.101 --> 51:05.854
I wonder if you'd look my way
if I killed him too.

51:09.524 --> 51:10.484
Would you?

51:11.610 --> 51:13.737
I would never let that happen.

51:18.909 --> 51:19.826
Then tell me.

51:20.535 --> 51:22.662
How am I so different from Han Jeong-won?

51:23.163 --> 51:24.206
Let go.

51:32.714 --> 51:33.548
Tell me.

51:35.592 --> 51:36.426
Why is it that--

51:36.510 --> 51:37.427
You bastard.

51:50.774 --> 51:51.608
Crazy bastard.

51:52.692 --> 51:53.527
Die.

51:54.653 --> 51:56.571
Die, you son of a bitch!

51:57.239 --> 51:58.323
Die!

51:58.406 --> 52:01.368
Stop it, Mr. Han Jeong-won.

52:02.410 --> 52:03.537
Mr. Han Jeong-won!

52:59.759 --> 53:02.596
You said you went to shooting ranges
with your father, but man!

53:03.180 --> 53:05.849
Didn't you say he dragged you there
against your will?

53:06.516 --> 53:08.852
You acted
like you'd never touch a gun again.

53:08.935 --> 53:09.895
What's gotten into you?

53:11.479 --> 53:14.107
Do you still have that gun in your house?

53:17.194 --> 53:19.321
That thing looked really cool,
your father's gun.

53:20.780 --> 53:22.199
You said it's not registered, right?

53:23.825 --> 53:24.659
Have you

53:26.077 --> 53:27.704
ever wanted to kill someone?

53:29.497 --> 53:30.332
Plenty of times.

53:30.874 --> 53:32.626
Sometimes, I feel like killing you.

53:36.922 --> 53:38.632
Is there someone you want to kill?

53:46.097 --> 53:49.726
CONFRONTATION
WITH DEPUTY MANAGER NOH IN-JI

53:57.067 --> 53:58.568
Deputy Manager Noh In-ji is here.

53:58.652 --> 53:59.736
Tell her to come in.

54:02.113 --> 54:04.199
PHYSICAL ALTERCATION
WITH CLIENT HAN JEONG-WON

54:17.545 --> 54:20.298
If this is about Eom Tae-seong,
we're looking for a solution.

54:21.424 --> 54:23.843
No. I'm here for something else.

54:26.763 --> 54:28.974
Once my marriage
with Mr. Han Jeong-won ends,

54:29.599 --> 54:30.976
I will be leaving the company.

54:32.811 --> 54:33.687
Is this

54:34.604 --> 54:36.147
because of Mr. Seo Do-ha?

54:36.773 --> 54:37.607
No.

54:38.566 --> 54:40.443
This concerns my productivity
as an employee.

54:42.237 --> 54:44.572
I don't think I'm fit
to continue this work.

54:44.656 --> 54:46.032
You couldn't be more wrong.

54:46.908 --> 54:49.494
None of our employees
have the results you do, Ms. Noh.

54:51.955 --> 54:54.457
My resignation
is also best for the company.

54:55.041 --> 54:58.461
Eom Tae-seong may put the company at risk.

54:59.254 --> 55:02.215
If I stop working here,
he might let things settle.

55:02.716 --> 55:04.134
If that's your reason,

55:04.801 --> 55:06.761
we'll do everything we can to stop him.

55:06.845 --> 55:08.388
My mind's already made up.

55:11.182 --> 55:13.018
I appreciate all you've done for me.

55:35.832 --> 55:37.500
Fricking vending machine coffee.

55:38.585 --> 55:39.711
This is the stuff.

55:39.794 --> 55:42.422
Yirgacheffe's always been my favorite.

55:44.174 --> 55:48.595
To think the CEO herself would come see me
over Noh In-ji's resignation.

55:51.890 --> 55:53.516
Why do you think she's quitting?

55:54.476 --> 55:56.186
Probably because of Eom Tae-seong.

55:57.437 --> 55:59.356
You should have killed him ages ago.

56:02.108 --> 56:03.068
I was only kidding.

56:03.151 --> 56:05.403
No need to scare me
with the silent treatment.

56:08.990 --> 56:11.618
This isn't her first time
dealing with Eom Tae-seong.

56:12.202 --> 56:13.870
I figured there was another reason.

56:13.953 --> 56:17.665
It seems things are completely over
between her and the owner of the house.

56:18.249 --> 56:21.961
Which leaves us with only one conclusion.
It's no longer strictly business for her.

56:22.837 --> 56:26.800
Sure, this business sets people up
with their ideal match,

56:26.883 --> 56:29.010
but a marriage still takes
some dedication.

56:29.594 --> 56:32.305
In the process,
couples may end up loathing each other,

56:32.389 --> 56:35.016
or they may actually develop feelings.

56:37.227 --> 56:41.314
Are you telling me she's doing this
over Mr. Han Jeong-won, not Eom Tae-seong?

56:41.398 --> 56:43.316
Want to hear it from someone

56:43.400 --> 56:45.402
who's been married
and divorced three times?

56:46.069 --> 56:48.863
Married couples can endure
physical hardships.

56:48.947 --> 56:51.491
What they can't endure
is a loveless relationship.

56:51.991 --> 56:54.119
Conversely, even a fake couple

56:54.744 --> 56:56.413
might struggle to suppress
genuine feelings.

56:56.496 --> 56:57.622
After all, they are married.

56:59.999 --> 57:02.585
Knowing Noh In-ji,
why do you think she's doing it?

57:03.837 --> 57:08.133
So she's resigning because she developed
actual feelings for a client?

57:13.930 --> 57:15.014
God, that's bitter.

58:21.623 --> 58:23.124
MR. KIM

58:26.294 --> 58:27.378
Yes, Mr. Kim.

58:52.487 --> 58:55.615
The CCTV installers we hired
discovered them.

58:56.866 --> 58:58.660
They were installed by experts.

59:00.078 --> 59:01.663
Shall I remove them right away?

59:34.404 --> 59:35.822
Come home right now.

59:37.198 --> 59:39.200
It appears Mr. Han Jeong-won knows
what you did.

59:54.966 --> 59:56.884
OPEN DOOR

01:00:13.276 --> 01:00:14.944
Can't you just let it slide?

01:00:17.405 --> 01:00:18.239
Where is it?

01:00:48.311 --> 01:00:51.648
RECENTLY ACCESSED
PAST SEVEN DAYS

01:02:05.304 --> 01:02:08.099
RECENT CALLS
NOH IN-JI

01:02:08.182 --> 01:02:10.268
We looked through Eom Tae-seong's gallery

01:02:10.852 --> 01:02:12.562
and found countless photos of you.

01:02:18.860 --> 01:02:20.194
Why didn't you report him?

01:02:24.449 --> 01:02:25.283
I did.

01:02:26.367 --> 01:02:27.201
Several times.

01:02:28.453 --> 01:02:31.914
But you wouldn't take action
unless someone had killed or been killed.

01:02:45.720 --> 01:02:46.971
…but got stabbed

01:02:47.555 --> 01:02:48.890
by Seo Do-ha.

01:02:48.973 --> 01:02:51.434
Thanks to him,
I ended up killing a random person.

01:02:52.602 --> 01:02:55.938
We found traces of Eom Tae-seong's blood,
and his prints were everywhere.

01:02:56.689 --> 01:03:00.485
The pharmacist's murder case was closed
as we couldn't prosecute Eom Tae-seong,

01:03:00.985 --> 01:03:02.779
what with him dying.

01:03:02.862 --> 01:03:06.324
But we have a duty to find criminals,
even if they did kill a murderer.

01:03:10.578 --> 01:03:12.914
We traced Eom Tae-seong's movements

01:03:13.414 --> 01:03:15.917
and found he was involved
with many people in your circle.

01:03:16.000 --> 01:03:17.960
For instance,
the break-in at Mr. Seo's home

01:03:18.461 --> 01:03:20.254
and the assault on Mr. Han.

01:03:24.050 --> 01:03:24.884
And?

01:03:28.679 --> 01:03:31.349
I've given some thought

01:03:31.432 --> 01:03:33.851
to who might want Eom Tae-seong gone.

01:03:37.897 --> 01:03:38.773
Ms. Noh In-ji,

01:03:40.107 --> 01:03:41.442
where were you that day?

01:03:54.747 --> 01:03:55.581
At the lake.

01:06:13.469 --> 01:06:16.889
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
